Part 8 — Native Android (NDK-Heavy) Application Reverse Engineering Methodology (Beginner → Expert)

This section will focus on applications where the majority of logic resides in native code. It will cover ELF binaries, JNI architecture, C/C++ execution models, dynamic linking, Android's native runtime, ABI-specific behavior, object lifecycles, memory layout, threading, native libraries, and reconstruction of complete native application architecture from Android packages.